    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "No disk on a Cloud Run service",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 3,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 8
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Cloud Run services have no disk.** A file a container writes is held in its memory, so a service's \"disk space\" is its **Memory** chart: files that grow show as memory climbing to the red line, then as a container killed for memory. Real disk is on the databases (each one's disk space is on its area's page and on Databases) and in the buckets. A **red line** is the line the pager uses (tpa-platform's alert policies); a **grey line** is a limit the service is set to.",
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        }
      },
      "id": 5
    },
